Fixed in round 70: a pack expansion whose pattern IS the bare pack
reference is now substituted element-wise in apply()'s template-argument
replication path ([temp.variadic]/5), instead of relying on the flat
map's short-name bridge -- which picked another live template's
same-named pack and left the replicas as the bare name, so every element
collapsed to the pack's first ((int*, int) became (int*, int*)).
Verified to FAIL (vacuous: main dropped, 0 assertions) with the fix
reverted.  Runtime-verified with g++ and clang++.
